ttbfp - CPU implementation of Tenstorrent block-float formats
=========================================================

The quantizer/dequantizer in `src/ttbfp_cpu.cpp` and
`python/ttbfp/reference.py` mirrors the packing rules of the Tenstorrent
tt-llk reference helpers (`pack.py`, `unpack.py`, `bfp_format_utils.py`):

  SPDX-FileCopyrightText: (c) 2025-2026 Tenstorrent AI ULC
  SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

The verbatim upstream helpers used for validation live in
`tools/verify_against_tt.py`. No tt-metal source is compiled or linked.

GPT-QModel changes:
  * CPU encode/decode plus a fused dequantize+GEMM (scalar, AVX2+FMA,
    AVX-512), with block-major and int8 kernel-native layouts
  * optional CUDA port of the same kernels (compile-checked only)
  * decoder-aware tile selection and a software-pipelined decode
  * 174-test bitwise parity suite and same-process A/B benchmark
